{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/28368-new-hunter-setting-hunter-wins","id":28368,"title":"New Hunter Setting: Hunter wins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-11T16:21:19-08:00","id":28368,"title":"New Hunter Setting: Hunter wins","content":"I just thought of this one A while ago thinking what would happen if all the hunters teamed up and cause a near destruction of all supernatural game lines. They still exist but their arent enough Supernatural races to left to build i.e Tribes, Orders, and Krewes. Which also means that their arent enough races left to do their duty for instance:<br /> <br /> WereWolf the foresaken: Spirits would go on A rampage with no one watching the borders Les Mysteries would also go extinct or be possessed by spirits with no one to stop them.<br /> <br /> Mage the awakening: Since mages are the only one who can fight off the abyss the world would be going under corruption by abyssal demons. Also what would the St George feel about that now realizing that they got it in reverse.<br /> <br /> Changeling the lost: Changelings are the only thing that can deal with true fae and also prevent them from taking anymore then the true fae can kidnap anyone they want their will still be changelings but not enough to make a court have been destroyed also I consider that the true fae would also hunt down the ones that killed their former escaped servants just a twist.<br /> <br /> Giest sin eater: this one took a while but since the destruction hit the other supernatural splats as well as them the left over sin eaters will have to deal with the hundreds of dead supernaturals the great hunt has caused. Also meaning that they have to talk or go straight to hunters since they caused the whole event.<br /> <br /> Also another thing to consider what will the hunters do now that they killed the only ones who can deal with the problem do they try to deal with it themselves or do they try to bring back the other supernaturals they have killed and hope to learn from their mistakes. The feeling should for this setting would be regret or fear at fighting the enemys only the other game-lines can deal with but also sorrow helps for killing dozens of innocent victims or supernaturals that they killed. Also this doesnt have to be a hunter game any other gameline can be just as playable but I believe the felling for this one as well should be loneliness since you are one of the few remaining vampires werewolves or other supernaturals left no one to help you deal with abyssal demons or spirits that now smash the border and are now going in. This especially helps if your pc is new to the whole giest or werewolf thing meaning that no one can tell them what to do( well your giest can tell you what you are but still can tell you what you are or what you have to do). <br /> <br /> So what do you guys think cool setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T16:31:56-08:00","id":28372,"title":"","content":"Some things to point out, aren't Mages also the leading cause of Abyssal corruption on the Phenomenal world? Not to mention you also just took out the Seers, that should help the world a bunch.<br /> <br /> Changelings are not the only ones who handle the True Fae, arguably Normal Humans and especially Hunters have been holding back the true fae, the whole bane issue and their vulnerability to iron has plain old been used likely more by the overwhelming number of humans then by changelings throughout history. And Hobgoblins are also things Hunters normally take on, though they probably don't know that the boogeyman they are lynching is a hobgoblin from the Hedge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So why did they only take out the PC splats? The World is crazy filled with much more monsters then PC Splats. Spirits alone could fill the world with enough trouble to keep the hunters busy not to mention nonmage witches, and ghosts/zombies, and Cryptids/Hobgoblins/other random monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T16:51:23-08:00","id":28383,"title":"","content":"I didnt take out only the splats I was only doing examples also you have a good point with the seers but the thing is while mages also cause Abyssal Corruption they also try to clean it up. Also while hunter do deal with the true fae most of the time changelings have a more thorough understanding on how true fae works. If I wanted to do all the world of darkness that would take a long time. I was saying what would happen if the hunter killed nearly all supernaturals creatures not just PC splats but also their enemy's and Allies minus some things like true fae and ghosts seeing as ghosts will always be a problem you could probably take out the fae but you need a hell of a fire power to take them all out but still. The setting Iam making is what would happen if the hunters finally got what they want a and what would happen next this my take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T17:03:11-08:00","id":28395,"title":"","content":"Well I always viewed that Conspiracies would be considered Monsters half the time by other Hunters. Seriously if I was a single lone hunter like Frank Castle, or average Joe Member of the Union and I found out that their was a conglomerate kidnapping monsters to graft monster powers to their kidnap teams, or a group of Devil Children or hell just a member of the Abbey I would consider them monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T18:34:32-08:00","id":28440,"title":"","content":"Point taken but most hunters sort tolerate each other and also you forgot mention slashers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T19:56:51-08:00","id":28481,"title":"","content":"1)You can only tolerate what you properly identify as human. If some guy looks like he might be wolfing out or has a entourage of corpses, then are you really going to stop and ask what they are before you shoot them? Odds are, probably not. You find out later that you just killed an employee of Cheiron or a Lucifuge(respectively).<br /> 2)He alluded to them with Ashwood Abbey. They may not be slashers per se, but it's not a long road for most. In fact, including Ashwood goes steps beyond slasher and into morally ambiguous grey technical 'innocents' getting murdered because of appearance.(I'm not saying the Abbey is innocent here, but not everyone of them is completely an asshole-some do their pleasure fairly humanely, or at least more decently than you'd expect from this lot)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T21:14:40-08:00","id":28522,"title":"","content":"Yeah that true the ashwood abbey are very immoral but they are nothing compared to the hunt club I am pretty sure I went a little to far by saying that all Conspiracies can team up I am pretty Cheirion, Lucifuge and Hunt Club would probably removed if the hunters ever do a pact together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T21:29:14-08:00","id":28526,"title":"","content":"Task Force Valkyrie has a fiction that implies that the TFV would be sent after other hunters.<br /> The Lucifuge might not have anything to do if they killed all the demons. Knights of St George would deal with remaining Abyssal spirits, but a lot of the groups would probably just retire (Talbot Group) or twist their clandestine power for their own purposes (Barrett Commission).<br /> <br /> It's an entirely reasonable idea for a setting, of course. But it really seems like you're just replacing known elements (werewolves and other playable splats) for lesser known elements (spirits and true fae and others). If you want the new hunters to deal with these opponents, they're going to have to develop special techniques (since it's hard for mortals to fight with spirits and the true fae) leading to different endowments, or place them on a reactive stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T05:59:29-08:00","id":28666,"title":"","content":"I'd stick to individual splats, having magi, werewolves and vamps all go extinct at once will either be overly complicated as their mythologies interact or risk being massively underwhelming.<br /> <br /> That being said...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WereWolf the foresaken: Spirits would go on A rampage with no one watching the borders Les Mysteries would also go extinct or be possessed by spirits with no one to stop them. </div> </div> </div>I think this is selling it short. The Uratha are the children of Luna, the rank 9 god after all. You could run it as a proper end times scenario with cataclysmic flooding and infectious madness in the population as the moon god decides to put humanity in it's place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T07:36:43-08:00","id":28716,"title":"","content":"a bunch of 'conspiracies' as varied and poisonous as what we have all forming a hunter justice league seems kind of unlikely and uninteresting honestly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T09:06:58-08:00","id":28757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/28368-new-hunter-setting-hunter-wins?p=28666#post28666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is selling it short. The Uratha are the children of Luna, the rank 9 god after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 8. Gaia is Rank 9, if she exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T09:41:54-08:00","id":28775,"title":"","content":"It remains a debate, even among the wisest Ithaeur, exactly what Rank some of these entities are supposed to be, and who outranks whom. This is almost certainly exactly the way the spirits like it.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has Luna and Helios as both rank 8 and 9. Unknown. Mage suggests rank 7.<br /> <br /> Either way, it boils down to spirits causing more trouble than usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-12-2013, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T13:31:18-08:00","id":28896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/28368-new-hunter-setting-hunter-wins?p=28775#post28775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It remains a debate, even among the wisest Ithaeur, exactly what Rank some of these entities are supposed to be, and who outranks whom. This is almost certainly exactly the way the spirits like it.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has Luna and Helios as both rank 8 and 9. Unknown. Mage suggests rank 7.<br /> <br /> Either way, it boils down to spirits causing more trouble than usual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage suggests Rank <i>8</i>, which happens to be the Rank that that game labels as Kings and Queens (when one of Luna's aspects is &quot;Queen of the Night) and the lower of the two Ranks Werewolf labels as Celestines (when Gaia's spread of placement is consistently higher than Luna or Helios and mythic resonance posits her seniority over those two without suggesting she's at Monad levels of you-cannot-grasp-the-true-formlessness a la Rank 10).<br /> <br /> It suggests Rank 7 for the Firstborn and the rest of the animal totems, which is flush with Lore of the Forsaken's statement that spirits can't get more powerful than greater Incarnae without a fundamental rearrangement of the universe.<br /> <br /> Luna possesses near-omniscience that nevertheless has notable holes in it and set in motion the perpetuation of roughly half a species of shapeshifters that bear her spiritual marks. Gaia's list of storied accomplishments is a bit shorter, but includes <i>raising the Gauntlet.</i><br /> <br /> A Rank 8 spirit being rendered unable to protect their assets is something of a disaster, but a Rank 9 spirit having the same happen would seem to indicate nothing less than a Class X apocalypse, at which point you have <i>much</i> bigger problems on your hands than malignant dickery from Jagglings and Incarnae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T14:21:38-08:00","id":28927,"title":"","content":"What you two actually disagreeing about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T18:48:04-08:00","id":29070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/28368-new-hunter-setting-hunter-wins?p=28927#post28927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you two actually disagreeing about?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know eighter their debating over power levels of werewolf and mage or are doing a ranking on apocalypses and what would happen if they were extinct","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 12-12-2013, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T03:00:35-08:00","id":29220,"title":"","content":"Am I wrong or very wrong? You decide!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T08:19:04-08:00","id":29325,"title":"","content":"Something that just occurred to me while reading Intruders...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> aren't Mages also the leading cause of Abyssal corruption on the Phenomenal world? </div> </div> </div>It would make a degree of sense but according to Intruders they aren't. The Abyss can insinuate itself anywhere in the world and most manifestations aren't directly connected to the Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T08:32:14-08:00","id":29336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/28368-new-hunter-setting-hunter-wins?p=28896#post28896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna possesses near-omniscience that nevertheless has notable holes in it and set in motion the perpetuation of roughly half a species of shapeshifters that bear her spiritual marks. Gaia's list of storied accomplishments is a bit shorter, but includes <i>raising the Gauntlet.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I always wondered why Luna/Helios was an awakened spirit while Gaia is &quot;not talking to morals&quot; in terms of nWoD lore.<br /> <br /> Then again, this more than likely was an attempt to back off the oWoD mindset.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T06:47:42-08:00","id":31622,"title":"","content":"I think it\u00b4s a fascinating premise, although it may be difficult to flesh it out (the existence of Monsters itself is the Raison d\u00b4etre for Hunter cells)<br /> Just some wild ideas that may work for this scenario, some may contradict each other:<br /> <br /> All Supernatural culture is extinct or reduced to a point where it does not matter anymore<br /> (Covenants, Tribes, Mage Legacies etc. are no longer game relevant)<br /> <br /> Hunters use different sorts of Supernaturals for their own purposes<br /> -Cheiron Group breeds them for harvesting organs<br /> -Network Zero employs Vampire Spies<br /> -Thule uses Geists and Wolfs to make guided tours into the Underworld and Shadow ...<br /> <br /> In order to defeat the Supernaturals the Hunters must have learned and adopted new tricks<br /> so you could include a lot of new abilities, weapons and roles for Hunters<br /> Shaman Hunters learning Gifts and stepping into the Shadow,<br /> Ghoul Hunters use farmed blood for power boost<br /> Hedge Wizard Hunters can learn basic rotes and spells<br /> <br /> After the decline of the Monsters Hunter Groups must find something to do...<br /> Conspiracies become offical firms or arms of government, Compacts become full-blown secret organizations<br /> Ashwood Abbey: Supernatural Safaris, Drugs<br /> TFV: building the Super-Soldier, winning the supernatural Cold War with othe gov conspiracies<br /> The Union: stop supernatural power abuse in Politics<br /> Thule: learn Magic, visit supernatural realms<br /> Cheiron: next century surgery and pharmaceuticals<br /> Network Zero: reveal the evil deeds of Cheiron and TFV<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T07:05:03-08:00","id":31634,"title":"","content":"So essentially the hunters will replace the supernatural creatures and start to hunt each other...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T10:30:57-08:00","id":31762,"title":"","content":"Almost like that, Hunters will become big Corporations and Government,<br /> Supernatural becomes a market and everyone wants a piece of the cake.<br /> <br /> so maybe more a mix between predatory capitalism, Cold War spy story and Mafia Mob war<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T16:05:55-08:00","id":37540,"title":"","content":"You either die fighting the monsters, or live long enough to see yourself become that which you fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}